                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7ff23376-f6f6-40bc-8df7-f2b08937c813",
                        "source_entry_id": "16fdc67d-6bf6-3ebf-ab2d-cef94a139898",
                        "target_lang_word": "baldrick",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "baldrick",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2060b010-4f8f-3a1f-8116-56ead9567375",
                                        "entry_id": "049925c6-71b8-382e-9887-d121347149d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of baldric."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dc6f53c-1d85-45b4-a8b5-a87c7259568e",
                                                "sense_id": "2060b010-4f8f-3a1f-8116-56ead9567375",
                                                "text": "And the bright green belt on his body he bore, oblique, like a baldrick, bound at his side below his left shoulder, laced in a knot..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d7a4492-7584-4180-a52d-6e9a6a884aca",
                                                "sense_id": "2060b010-4f8f-3a1f-8116-56ead9567375",
                                                "text": "That a woman conceiv'd me, I thank her; that she brought me up, I likewise give her most humble thanks; but that I will have a rechate winded in my forehead, or hang my bugle in an invisible baldrick, all women shall pardon me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf1bbf6e-5a43-4fd2-a793-0c362a57e4c1",
                                                "sense_id": "2060b010-4f8f-3a1f-8116-56ead9567375",
                                                "text": "And from his blazoned baldrick slung, a mighty silver bugle hung..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24bb6a93-07cb-420e-8d96-9c7390860f75",
                                                "sense_id": "2060b010-4f8f-3a1f-8116-56ead9567375",
                                                "text": "The sword was carried in a belt of buff or other leather girded round the body, or thrown over the right shoulder, these shoulder belts were called baudricks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60091cff-6f12-432d-a9a9-31d6b55a4ccc",
                        "source_entry_id": "16fdc67d-6bf6-3ebf-ab2d-cef94a139898",
                        "target_lang_word": "baldric",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "baldric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                        "entry_id": "96da2e6f-f064-33ea-a76c-a2e72a0915f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A broad belt, originally of leather and often richly ornamented, worn diagonally from shoulder to hip (across the breast and under the opposite arm), which was formerly used to hold a sword, a bugle, etc., and is now chiefly worn for ceremonial purposes; also (loosely), any belt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3034872-e93a-48f8-8bfb-78ed0c851339",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "But now how many men are there proude of that that is not theyrs at al? Is there no man proude of keping another mannes gate? […] [W]hat a brag-kyng maketh a beareward wͭ [with] his ſyluer buttened bawdrike, for pride of another mannes bere?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "811f307d-48f7-48cd-a399-b638f7a13d69",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "Athvvart his breſt a bauldrick braue he vvare, / That ſhind, like tvvinkling ſtars, vvith ſtones moſt pretious rare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ca4620f-d265-4d55-91a4-186390c91d4a",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "[B]ut that I vvill haue a rechate vvinded in my forehead, or hang my bugle in an inuiſible baldricke, all vvomen ſhall pardon mee: becauſe I vvill not doe them the vvrong to miſtruſt any, I vvill doe my ſelfe the right to truſt none: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59f26618-7af5-48c1-b65b-45742cd71320",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "A radiant Baldric, o'er his Shoulder ty'd, / Suſtains the Svvord that glitters at his ſide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5deba64-11e9-44c5-8406-58824723564c",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "And from his blazon'd baldric slung, / A mighty silver bugle hung, / And, as he rode, his armour rung, / Beside remote Shalott."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7790952-e6ca-4fe6-ae12-98715191ffda",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "Fore George, I would not ask thee to buckle my baldrick when the war-steeds were snorting, but I would trust Isabel with the links of my hauberk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "518fa897-dfde-4734-aa43-18033bd31df5",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "The longer weapon is carried by a narrow bauldric slung over the right shoulder and meeting another cord-shaped band at the breast, in fact suggesting our antiquated cross-belts. The Sword is always worn on the left side. […] A soldier's bauldric is coloured red, like the wood of the bows and arrows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b26c6d50-a3ce-4181-a32f-d9747d83c581",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "The figure on the left, holding the severed head of the ox, has removed his sword with the baldric from which it is suspended and given it to his companion, who holds it beside his own with the baldric swinging."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432a6c95-c28a-49b3-91c9-96a9eea68291",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "The man facing Locklear had his head covered with a red bandanna, and over his shoulder was a baldric from which a cutlass had hung. The cutlass was now carving through the air at Locklear's head."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c80ebbc-9652-49c2-9a6f-ff626d39a3ec",
                                                "sense_id": "a524997d-08e6-3ffd-9b95-103f1d167526",
                                                "text": "The face of the man who stood before him was hidden by a Corinthian helmet. His bronze breastplate was decorated in silver, and he carried his sword hanging from a chain-mail baldric. Over his shoulders was a cloak of blue linen that the evening breeze filled like a sail."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91fa2e3f-0037-326f-826a-6437b53bb758",
                                        "entry_id": "96da2e6f-f064-33ea-a76c-a2e72a0915f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A (usually leather) strap from which the clapper of a bell is suspended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e04963b-c074-4056-964b-6111e755bcd1",
                                                "sense_id": "91fa2e3f-0037-326f-826a-6437b53bb758",
                                                "text": "[P]aid to the Collermaker of Leawsam for a bawdricke for the great bell … … … iijs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4000b483-b110-4953-9d8c-7a3237776cc3",
                                                "sense_id": "91fa2e3f-0037-326f-826a-6437b53bb758",
                                                "text": "The Bawdricke of a bell-clapper. Ropalicorigia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776ab26f-f7f9-43af-bd9e-cdc0856b4f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "91fa2e3f-0037-326f-826a-6437b53bb758",
                                                "text": "The Bells were evidently a constant source of expense, and very large sums were spent in their re-casting and re-hanging. Scarcely a year passed without some new bell-wheel, bawdricke, rope or clapper being required."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc450373-dee3-338f-aaa8-cd3afea7acbb",
                                        "entry_id": "96da2e6f-f064-33ea-a76c-a2e72a0915f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A necklace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
